A simple solution is to generate all binary sequences of length 2n and count the number of sequences such that sum of first n bits is same as sum of last n bits.

An efficient solution is to use dynamic programming. Let dp[i][j] be the number of binary sequences of length i such that sum of first j bits is same as sum of last j bits.

The base cases are dp[0][0] = 1 and dp[i][0] = 1 for all i.

The recurrence relation is dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1] + dp[i-1][j] for all i > 0 and j > 0.

The final answer is dp[2n][n].

The time complexity of the above solution is O(n^2).

The space complexity is O(n^2).

